"""Redfish–StarlingX Asset Identity & API/Dashboard Integration Validation — Phase 28G.

Validates that the Redfish legacy pipeline and the StarlingX canonical pipeline
maintain correct asset identity semantics, and that no unauthorized identity
inference (name/IP-based matching) occurs.

Pipeline under test:
    StarlingXProviderAdapter(fixture)
        → StarlingXProviderNormalizer
        → CanonicalInventory (Node, Platform, Cluster — NO Physical)
        → HealthService / FaultDetectionService / AlertService
        → GraphBuilder

Test scenarios:
    1. bm_type/bm_ip/bm_hostname preservation in Node metadata
    2. bm_type=none → no Physical entity created
    3. No graph edges from name/IP similarity
    4. FM Critical and Redfish Critical remain separate faults
    5. Serial/UUID mismatch → separate entities maintained
    6. Missing identification → separate entities, no auto-merge
    7. Hostname/IP-only match → NOT treated as same asset
    8. Management API handles both providers without regression
    9. Graph builder follows existing rules (DIRECT/DERIVED only)
    10. UNKNOWN is not converted to HEALTHY
    11. Node ≠ Physical — semantic boundary preserved
    12. Node.physical_ref is None when no Physical evidence
"""
